IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2021: civil penalties and disqualification of retail food stores and wholesale food concerns.
-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively). Same reading of results as snap4-s2020-a-d.l4: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING.
-- "Wholesale food concern" has no definition in section 2012: whether a seller is one is a fact the caller states (PLAN.md, difficulty 2).
-- The text is the converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

§ `s 2021(a) Disqualification`

DECLARE `s 2021(a)(1) sanction` IS ONE OF
    `s 2021(a)(1)(A) disqualification for a specified period of time from further participation`
    `s 2021(a)(1)(B) a civil penalty of up to $100,000 for each violation`
    `s 2021(a)(1)(C) both`
    `s 2021(a)(1) some other sanction`

-- src:1705 | An approved retail food store or wholesale food concern that violates a provision of this chapter or a regulation under this chapter may be—
-- src:1706 | (A) disqualified for a specified period of time from further participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program;
-- src:1707 | (B) assessed a civil penalty of up to $100,000 for each violation; or
-- src:1708 | (C) both.
-- jural: the Secretary | an approved retail food store or wholesale food concern | power and liability: disqualification, a civil penalty, or both
@ref s 2021(a)(1) (src:1705-1708)
GIVEN `s 2018 the seller is an approved retail food store or wholesale food concern` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the seller violates a provision of this chapter or a regulation under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanction` IS A `s 2021(a)(1) sanction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(a)(1) the seller may be subjected to the sanction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2018 the seller is an approved retail food store or wholesale food concern`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the seller is approved is section 2018's answer and was not supplied
    WHEN JUST approved THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT (approved AND `the seller violates a provision of this chapter or a regulation under this chapter`)
                THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An approved retail food store or wholesale food concern that violates a provision of this chapter or a regulation under this chapter may be"
            IF `the sanction` EQUALS `s 2021(a)(1) some other sanction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names disqualification, a civil penalty, or both
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 2021(a)(1)(B) (src:1707)
GIVEN `the civil penalty for the violation, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(a)(1)(B) the civil penalty for each violation is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the civil penalty for the violation, in dollars` AT MOST 100000 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "assessed a civil penalty of up to $100,000 for each violation"

DECLARE `s 2021(a)(2) evidence` IS ONE OF
    `s 2021(a)(2) facts established through on-site investigations`
    `s 2021(a)(2) inconsistent redemption data`
    `s 2021(a)(2) evidence obtained through a transaction report under an electronic benefit transfer system`
    `s 2021(a)(2) any other evidence`

-- src:1710 | Regulations promulgated under this chapter shall provide criteria for the finding of a violation of, the suspension or disqualification of and the assessment of a civil penalty against a retail food store or wholesale food concern on the basis of evidence that may include facts established through on-site investigations, inconsistent redemption data, or evidence obtained through a transaction report under an electronic benefit transfer system.
-- jural: a retail food store or wholesale food concern | the Secretary | immunity: findings of violation rest on regulatory criteria and evidence that may include three kinds
@ref s 2021(a)(2) (src:1710)
GIVEN `the evidence` IS A `s 2021(a)(2) evidence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(a)(2) the finding of a violation may rest on the evidence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the evidence`
    WHEN `s 2021(a)(2) any other evidence` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "on the basis of evidence that may include"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 2021(b) Period of disqualification`

DECLARE `s 2021(b) disqualification the text requires` IS ONE OF
    `s 2021(b) a reasonable period of time not exceeding the maximum` HAS `the maximum in years` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2021(b) permanent`
    `s 2021(b)(4) a reasonable period of time determined by the Secretary, including permanent`

-- src:1712 | Subject to subsection (c), a disqualification under subsection (a) shall be—
-- src:1713 | (1) for a reasonable period of time, not to exceed 5 years, upon the first occasion of disqualification;
-- src:1714 | (2) for a reasonable period of time, not to exceed 10 years, upon the second occasion of disqualification;
-- src:1716 | (A) the third occasion of disqualification;
-- src:1717 | (B) the first occasion or any subsequent occasion of a disqualification based on the purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or authorization cards by a retail food store or wholesale food concern or a finding of the unauthorized redemption, use, transfer, acquisition, alteration, or possession of EBT cards, except that the Secretary shall have the discretion to impose a civil penalty of up to $20,000 for each violation (except that the amount of civil penalties imposed for violations occurring during a single investigation may not exceed $40,000) in lieu of disqualification under this subparagraph, for such purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or cards that constitutes a violation of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter, if the Secretary determines that there is substantial evidence that such store or food concern had an effective policy and program in effect to prevent violations of the chapter and the regulations, including evidence that—
-- src:1722 | (C) a finding of the sale of firearms, ammunition, explosives, or controlled substance (as defined in section 802 of title 21) for coupons, except that the Secretary shall have the discretion to impose a civil penalty of up to $20,000 for each violation (except that the amount of civil penalties imposed for violations occurring during a single investigation may not exceed $40,000) in lieu of disqualification under this subparagraph if the Secretary determines that there is substantial evidence (including evidence that neither the ownership nor management of the store or food concern was aware of, approved, benefited from, or was involved in the conduct or approval of the violation) that the store or food concern had an effective policy and program in effect to prevent violations of this chapter; and
-- src:1723 | (4) for a reasonable period of time to be determined by the Secretary, including permanent disqualification, on the knowing submission of an application for the approval or reauthorization to accept and redeem coupons that contains false information about a substantive matter that was a part of the application.
-- jural: a retail food store or wholesale food concern | the Secretary | liability: the length of disqualification turns on the occasion and the ground
-- fork: F-2 | 1713 | the tiers of (1)-(2) and ground (4) can both apply to a first or second disqualification for a false application; chosen reading: the specific ground (4) governs (the Secretary determines the period, permanent included); the other reading: (1)/(2) cap it at 5 or 10 years
-- fork: F-2 | 1714 | see F-2 at 1713
-- fork: F-2 | 1723 | see F-2 at 1713; a third occasion is permanent under (3)(A) on either reading
@ref s 2021(b) (src:1712-1723)
GIVEN `the occasion of disqualification (1 for the first)` IS A NUMBER
      `the disqualification is based on the purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or authorization cards, or on the unauthorized redemption, use, transfer, acquisition, alteration, or possession of EBT cards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disqualification is based on a finding of the sale of firearms, ammunition, explosives, or controlled substances for coupons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disqualification is based on the knowing submission of an application containing false information about a substantive matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 2021(b) disqualification the text requires`
`s 2021(b) the disqualification the text requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the occasion of disqualification (1 for the first)` AT LEAST 3 THEN JUST `s 2021(b) permanent`
        IF `the disqualification is based on the purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or authorization cards, or on the unauthorized redemption, use, transfer, acquisition, alteration, or possession of EBT cards` THEN JUST `s 2021(b) permanent`
        IF `the disqualification is based on a finding of the sale of firearms, ammunition, explosives, or controlled substances for coupons` THEN JUST `s 2021(b) permanent`
        IF `the disqualification is based on the knowing submission of an application containing false information about a substantive matter` THEN JUST `s 2021(b)(4) a reasonable period of time determined by the Secretary, including permanent`
        IF `the occasion of disqualification (1 for the first)` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (`s 2021(b) a reasonable period of time not exceeding the maximum` 10)
        IF `the occasion of disqualification (1 for the first)` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST (`s 2021(b) a reasonable period of time not exceeding the maximum` 5)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text counts occasions of disqualification from the first
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2021(b) (src:1712-1714)
GIVEN `the occasion of disqualification (1 for the first)` IS A NUMBER
      `the disqualification is based on the purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or authorization cards, or on the unauthorized redemption, use, transfer, acquisition, alteration, or possession of EBT cards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disqualification is based on a finding of the sale of firearms, ammunition, explosives, or controlled substances for coupons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disqualification is based on the knowing submission of an application containing false information about a substantive matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is a reasonable period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period imposed` IS A `Period of ineligibility`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(b) the period imposed is allowed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2021(b) the disqualification the text requires` `the occasion of disqualification (1 for the first)` `the disqualification is based on the purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or authorization cards, or on the unauthorized redemption, use, transfer, acquisition, alteration, or possession of EBT cards` `the disqualification is based on a finding of the sale of firearms, ammunition, explosives, or controlled substances for coupons` `the disqualification is based on the knowing submission of an application containing false information about a substantive matter`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no disqualification is required for an occasion the text does not count
    WHEN JUST required THEN
        CONSIDER required
        WHEN `s 2021(b) permanent` THEN
            CONSIDER `the period imposed`
            WHEN permanently THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `for a number of days` d THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(3) permanent upon"
            WHEN `for a number of months` m THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(3) permanent upon"
            WHEN `for a number of years` y THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(3) permanent upon"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period is left to a condition, the Secretary or the State agency
        WHEN `s 2021(b) a reasonable period of time not exceeding the maximum` maxYears THEN
            IF NOT `the period is a reasonable period of time` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a reasonable period of time"
            ELSE
                CONSIDER `the period imposed`
                WHEN permanently THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not to exceed 5 years" and "not to exceed 10 years"
                WHEN `for a number of years` y THEN JUST (y AT MOST maxYears)
                WHEN `for a number of months` m THEN JUST (m AT MOST (maxYears TIMES 12))
                WHEN `for a number of days` d THEN
                    -- Any run of up to 365 days a year fits; no run of more than 366 days a year plus one does. Between the two, it depends on the day the disqualification begins.
                    BRANCH
                        IF d AT MOST (maxYears TIMES 365) THEN JUST TRUE
                        IF d GREATER THAN ((maxYears TIMES 366) PLUS 1) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not to exceed 5 years" and "not to exceed 10 years"
                        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives no day on which the disqualification begins, so a count of days between the two bounds may or may not exceed the years
                OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period is left to a condition, the Secretary or the State agency
        WHEN `s 2021(b)(4) a reasonable period of time determined by the Secretary, including permanent` THEN
            IF NOT `the period is a reasonable period of time` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a reasonable period of time to be determined by the Secretary"
            ELSE
                CONSIDER `the period imposed`
                WHEN permanently THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `for a number of years` y THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `for a number of months` m THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `for a number of days` d THEN JUST TRUE
                OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period is left to a condition, a regulation or the State agency

-- src:1717 | except that the Secretary shall have the discretion to impose a civil penalty of up to $20,000 for each violation (except that the amount of civil penalties imposed for violations occurring during a single investigation may not exceed $40,000) in lieu of disqualification under this subparagraph, for such purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or cards that constitutes a violation of the provisions of this chapter or the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter, if the Secretary determines that there is substantial evidence …
-- jural: a retail food store or wholesale food concern | the Secretary | power and liability: a civil penalty of up to $20,000 in lieu of permanent disqualification for trafficking
@ref s 2021(b)(3)(B) (src:1717)
GIVEN `the violation is a purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or cards that constitutes a violation of this chapter or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that there is substantial evidence that the store or food concern had an effective policy and program in effect to prevent violations of the chapter and the regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the evidence includes that the ownership was not aware of, did not approve of, did not benefit from, and was not involved in the conduct of the violation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence includes that the management was not aware of, did not approve of, did not benefit from, and was not involved in the conduct of the violation, or was aware of or involved in the conduct of no more than 1 previous violation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(b)(3)(B) the Secretary may impose a civil penalty in lieu of permanent disqualification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary determines that there is substantial evidence that the store or food concern had an effective policy and program in effect to prevent violations of the chapter and the regulations`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Secretary's determination was not supplied
    WHEN JUST determined THEN
      IF NOT `the violation is a purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or cards that constitutes a violation of this chapter or the regulations` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for such purchase of coupons or trafficking in coupons or cards that constitutes a violation of the provisions of this chapter"
      ELSE
        BRANCH
            IF NOT determined THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary determines that there is substantial evidence that such store or food concern had an effective policy and program in effect to prevent violations"
            IF `the evidence includes that the ownership was not aware of, did not approve of, did not benefit from, and was not involved in the conduct of the violation`
                AND `the evidence includes that the management was not aware of, did not approve of, did not benefit from, and was not involved in the conduct of the violation, or was aware of or involved in the conduct of no more than 1 previous violation` THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including evidence that"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

