-- src:1742 | At any time after a civil penalty imposed under paragraph (1) has become final under the provisions of section 2023(a) of this title, the Secretary may request the Attorney General to institute a civil action against the person or persons subject to the penalty in a district court of the United States for any district in which such person or persons are found, reside, or transact business to collect the penalty …
-- jural: the Secretary | the Attorney General | power: a civil action in a district court to collect the final penalty
@ref s 2021(e)(2) (src:1742)
GIVEN `the civil penalty imposed under paragraph (1) has become final under section 2023(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(e)(2) the Secretary may request the Attorney General to institute a civil action to collect the penalty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the civil penalty imposed under paragraph (1) has become final under section 2023(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At any time after a civil penalty imposed under paragraph (1) has become final"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1742 | In such action, the validity and amount of such penalty shall not be subject to review.
-- jural: the persons subject to the penalty | the court | disability of the court: it may not review the validity or amount of the penalty
@ref s 2021(e)(2) (src:1742)
GIVEN `the action is one under paragraph (2) to collect a final civil penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(e)(2) the validity and amount of the penalty are subject to review in the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is one under paragraph (2) to collect a final civil penalty`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In such action, the validity and amount of such penalty shall not be subject to review"
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such action"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1743 | (3) The Secretary may impose a fine against any retail food store or wholesale food concern that accepts food coupons that are not accompanied by the corresponding book cover, other than the denomination of coupons used for making change as specified in regulations issued under this chapter. The amount of any such fine shall be established by the Secretary and may be assessed and collected in accordance with regulations issued under this chapter separately or in combination with any fiscal claim established by the Secretary. The Attorney General of the United States may institute judicial action in any court of competent jurisdiction against the store or concern to collect the fine.
-- jural: the Secretary | a retail food store or wholesale food concern that accepts loose coupons | power and liability: a fine, with judicial action by the Attorney General to collect it
@ref s 2021(e)(3) (src:1743)
GIVEN `the store or concern accepts food coupons that are not accompanied by the corresponding book cover` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coupons are of the denomination used for making change as specified in regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(e)(3) the Secretary may impose a fine against the store or concern` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the store or concern accepts food coupons that are not accompanied by the corresponding book cover` AND `the coupons are of the denomination used for making change as specified in regulations`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "food coupons that are not accompanied by the corresponding book cover, other than the denomination of coupons used for making change as specified in regulations"
        IF `the store or concern accepts food coupons that are not accompanied by the corresponding book cover` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any retail food store or wholesale food concern that accepts food coupons that are not accompanied by the corresponding book cover"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2021(f) Fines for unauthorized acceptance`

-- src:1745 | The Secretary may impose a fine against any person not approved by the Secretary to accept and redeem food coupons who violates any provision of this chapter or a regulation issued under this chapter, including violations concerning the acceptance of food coupons. The amount of any such fine shall be established by the Secretary and may be assessed and collected in accordance with regulations issued under this chapter separately or in combination with any fiscal claim established by the Secretary. The Attorney General of the United States may institute judicial action in any court of competent jurisdiction against the person to collect the fine.
-- jural: the Secretary | a person not approved to accept and redeem food coupons | power and liability: a fine for a violation, with judicial action by the Attorney General to collect it
@ref s 2021(f) (src:1745)
GIVEN `the person is not approved by the Secretary to accept and redeem food coupons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person violates a provision of this chapter or a regulation issued under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(f) the Secretary may impose a fine against the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is not approved by the Secretary to accept and redeem food coupons` AND `the person violates a provision of this chapter or a regulation issued under this chapter` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person not approved by the Secretary to accept and redeem food coupons who violates any provision of this chapter or a regulation issued under this chapter"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2021(g) Disqualification of retailers who are disqualified under WIC program`

-- inert: 1747-1748 | reason 2 | (g)(1) "The Secretary shall issue regulations providing criteria for the disqualification under this chapter of an approved retail food store or a wholesale food concern that is disqualified from accepting benefits under the special supplemental nutrition program for women, infants, and children": a regulation-making duty; the criteria are not in the Act

-- src:1749 | (2) Terms
-- src:1750 | A disqualification under paragraph (1)—
-- src:1751 | (A) shall be for the same length of time as the disqualification from the program referred to in paragraph (1);
-- jural: the Secretary | a store or concern disqualified under the WIC program | liability: the same length of disqualification
@ref s 2021(g)(2)(A) (src:1749-1751)
GIVEN `the period of the disqualification from the program referred to in paragraph (1)` IS A `Period of ineligibility`
GIVETH A `Period of ineligibility`
-- A period fixed by the text: the same length of time as the disqualification from the WIC program.
`s 2021(g)(2)(A) the length of the disqualification under this chapter` MEANS `the period of the disqualification from the program referred to in paragraph (1)`

-- src:1752 | (B) may begin at a later date than the disqualification from the program referred to in paragraph (1); and
-- jural: the Secretary | a store or concern disqualified under the WIC program | power: the disqualification may begin at a later date
@ref s 2021(g)(2)(B) (src:1752)
GIVEN `the day the disqualification under this chapter begins` IS A DATE
      `the day the disqualification from the program referred to in paragraph (1) begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(g)(2)(B) the disqualification under this chapter may begin on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day the disqualification under this chapter begins` GREATER THAN `the day the disqualification from the program referred to in paragraph (1) begins` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says it "may begin at a later date" and does not say whether it may begin on the same day or earlier
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1753 | (C) notwithstanding section 2023 of this title, shall not be subject to judicial or administrative review.
-- jural: a store or concern disqualified under paragraph (1) | the Secretary and the courts | disability: no judicial or administrative review, notwithstanding section 2023
@ref s 2021(g)(2)(C) (src:1753)
GIVEN `the disqualification is one under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(g)(2)(C) the disqualification is subject to judicial or administrative review` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disqualification is one under paragraph (1)`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "notwithstanding section 2023 of this title, shall not be subject to judicial or administrative review"
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A disqualification under paragraph (1)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2021(h) Flagrant violations`

-- src:1756 | The Secretary, in consultation with the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture, shall establish procedures under which the processing of program benefit redemptions for a retail food store or wholesale food concern may be immediately suspended pending administrative action to disqualify the retail food store or wholesale food concern.
-- jural: retail food stores and wholesale food concerns | the Secretary | power and liability: procedures for immediately suspending the processing of redemptions pending administrative action
