§ `s 2021(i) Pilot projects to improve Federal-State cooperation in identifying and reducing fraud`

-- src:1768 | The Secretary shall carry out, under such terms and conditions as are determined by the Secretary, pilot projects to test innovative Federal-State partnerships to identify, investigate, and reduce fraud by retail food stores and wholesale food concerns in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including allowing States to operate programs to investigate that fraud.
-- jural: the Secretary | State agencies | power: pilot projects with Federal-State partnerships against fraud by retail food stores and wholesale food concerns
@ref s 2021(i)(1)(A) (src:1768)
GIVEN `the project is a pilot project to test innovative Federal-State partnerships to identify, investigate, and reduce fraud by retail food stores and wholesale food concerns in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(i)(1)(A) the Secretary must carry out the pilot project` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the project is a pilot project to test innovative Federal-State partnerships to identify, investigate, and reduce fraud by retail food stores and wholesale food concerns in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "pilot projects to test innovative Federal-State partnerships to identify, investigate, and reduce fraud by retail food stores and wholesale food concerns"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1770 | At least 1 pilot project described in subparagraph (A) shall be carried out in an urban area that is among the 10 largest urban areas in the United States (based on population), if—
-- src:1771 | (i) the supplemental nutrition assistance program is separately administered in the area; and
-- src:1772 | (ii) if the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the area complies with the other applicable requirements of the program.
-- jural: the Secretary | the largest urban areas | claim and duty: at least 1 pilot project in an urban area among the 10 largest, if its program is separately administered and compliant
@ref s 2021(i)(1)(B) (src:1770-1772)
GIVEN `the area is an urban area that is among the 10 largest urban areas in the United States (based on population)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supplemental nutrition assistance program is separately administered in the area` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administration of the program in the area complies with the other applicable requirements of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2021(i)(1)(B) at least 1 pilot project must be carried out in the area` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the area is an urban area that is among the 10 largest urban areas in the United States (based on population)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in an urban area that is among the 10 largest urban areas in the United States (based on population)"
        IF NOT `the supplemental nutrition assistance program is separately administered in the area` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if— (i) the supplemental nutrition assistance program is separately administered in the area"
        IF NOT `the administration of the program in the area complies with the other applicable requirements of the program` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) if the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the area complies with the other applicable requirements of the program"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 2021(i)(2) selection criterion` IS ONE OF
    `s 2021(i)(2)(A) enhancing existing efforts by the Secretary to reduce fraud`
    `s 2021(i)(2)(B) requiring participant States to maintain the overall level of effort at addressing recipient fraud`
    `s 2021(i)(2)(C) collaborating with other law enforcement authorities as necessary`
    `s 2021(i)(2)(D) commitment of the participant State agency to follow Federal rules and procedures with respect to investigations`
    `s 2021(i)(2)(E) the extent to which a State has committed resources to recipient fraud and the relative success of those efforts`
    `s 2021(i)(2) any other criterion`

-- src:1774 | Pilot projects shall be selected based on criteria the Secretary establishes, which shall include—
-- src:1775 | (A) enhancing existing efforts by the Secretary to reduce fraud described in paragraph (1)(A);
-- src:1776 | (B) requiring participant States to maintain the overall level of effort of the States at addressing recipient fraud, as determined by the Secretary, prior to participation in the pilot project;
-- src:1777 | (C) collaborating with other law enforcement authorities as necessary to carry out an effective pilot project;
-- src:1778 | (D) commitment of the participant State agency to follow Federal rules and procedures with respect to investigations described in paragraph (1)(A); and
-- src:1779 | (E) the extent to which a State has committed resources to recipient fraud and the relative success of those efforts.
@ref s 2021(i)(2) (src:1774-1779)
